.TH "DAHARNESS\-INDEX" "1" "" "daharness 0.1.0" "daharness manual"
.SH NAME
daharness\-index \(em build or refresh the semantic tool\-registry index
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]daharness\-index\f[R] [\-\-clear] [\-\-chat]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The packaged deb ships an \f[B]empty\f[R] tool registry: the chroma
collection \f[CR]tool_inventory\f[R] starts unpopulated and nothing
fills it for you (the services daemon never indexes \(em indexing was
removed from its boot path deliberately).
\f[B]daharness\-index\f[R] is the operator\(aqs one\-typing pass that
builds it: discovery (static AST sweep + \f[CR]\(atframework_tool\f[R]
dynamic scan) over the installed tree, embedding of every manifest
through Ollama, and upsert into the chroma collection that every
discovery lane reads \(em \f[I]tools/search\f[R],
\f[I]tools/execute\f[R] (exact\-id and semantic), \f[I]/mcp\f[R]
\f[I]tools/list\f[R], the operator REPL, and memory recall.
.PP
Before doing any work it probes its two live dependencies and prints the
exact fix rather than a traceback: the vendored chroma server
(daharness\-chroma.service) and the Ollama host with the embed model
(default \f[B]nomic\-embed\-text\f[R]).
Probe knobs are read from /etc/daharness/daharness.env (CHROMA_PORT,
EMBED_MODEL, OLLAMA_BASE_URL), so a conffile retune is honored.
The indexer writes only through the chroma HTTP server, so it runs as
\f[B]any user\f[R] \(em no sudo needed (unless your conffile points at
something privileged).
.PP
Re\-runs are idempotent (upsert by tool id): newly added tools appear
without rebuilding.
\f[B]\-\-clear\f[R] wipes the collection first, for from\-scratch
rebuilds.
Embedding the \(ti97\-tool universe takes on the order of a minute
against a local Ollama host.
.PP
An empty or stale registry is not an error for the gateway \(em
\f[I]tools/search\f[R] just finds nothing and \f[I]tools/execute\f[R]
404s an unknown \f[I]tool_id\f[R], which is exactly what a fresh install
looks like before this command has run once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-clear\f[R]
Delete the collection contents before re\-indexing.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-chat\f[R]
Drop into the in\-tree interactive secretary chat lane instead of
indexing (dev\-tree convenience; the packaged headless build has no chat
model consumer).
.SH FILES
/etc/daharness/daharness.env \(em read (tolerantly) for the probe knobs.
